---
import ModuleRail from "./ModuleRail.astro";
import RankedChapters from "./RankedChapters.astro";
import DataDownload from "./DataDownload.astro";
import chapterData from "../../data/paper/m4_chapters.json";
import { fmtMag, fmtPct, type Estimate, type Lang } from "./chart-utils";
import { MODULES, SECTION_BASE, modulePath } from "../../data/outreach";

interface Props {
  lang: Lang;
}
const { lang } = Astro.props;

type Row = Estimate & {
  chapter: string;
  chapter_label_en: string;
  chapter_label_es: string;
  baseline_mean: number;
};
const rows = chapterData as Row[];
const lab = (r: Row) => (lang === "es" ? r.chapter_label_es : r.chapter_label_en);

/* Cold, cumulated over 30 days: the state the chart opens on. */
const coldCum = rows
  .filter((r) => r.bin === "-15_10" && r.horizon === 30)
  .sort((a, b) => a.pct - b.pct);

const mostDown = coldCum[0];
const mostUp = coldCum[coldCum.length - 1];
const respiratory = coldCum.find((r) => r.chapter === "respiratory")!;
const rising = coldCum.filter((r) => r.pct > 0);
const busiest = [...coldCum].sort((a, b) => b.baseline_mean - a.baseline_mean)[0];

const n = {
  mostDownLabel: lab(mostDown).toLowerCase(),
  mostDown: fmtMag(mostDown.pct),
  mostUpLabel: lab(mostUp).toLowerCase(),
  mostUp: fmtMag(mostUp.pct),
  respiratory: fmtPct(respiratory.pct),
  respiratoryBase: respiratory.baseline_mean.toFixed(1),
  risingCount: String(rising.length),
  totalCount: String(coldCum.length),
  busiestLabel: lab(busiest).toLowerCase(),
  busiestBase: busiest.baseline_mean.toFixed(1),
};

const self = MODULES.find((m) => m.id === "conditions")!;
const next = MODULES.find((m) => m.id === "projections")!;

const strings = {
  en: {
    eyebrow: self.short.en,
    h1: self.question.en,
    standfirst: `The fall in total visits on cold days is a net figure, and the net hides two opposite movements. Over 30 days after a day below 10 °C, ${n.mostDownLabel} visits fall by ${n.mostDown} while respiratory visits rise by ${n.respiratory}.`,
    fig1: "Every diagnostic chapter, at the interval and horizon you choose",
    readTitle: "What to read here",
    read: [
      `The aggregate is not the operational picture. ${n.risingCount} of ${n.totalCount} chapters move up on cold days over 30 days, even though the total moves down. Planning from the headline number alone would point a service in the wrong direction.`,
      `Respiratory is the chapter that rises, and it is a high-volume one: ${n.respiratory} over 30 days on a baseline of ${n.respiratoryBase} visits per 100,000. A percentage on a common condition is a larger absolute load than the same percentage on a rare one, which is why baseline volume sits next to every label.`,
      `The largest percentage belongs to ${n.mostDownLabel}, at ${n.mostDown}. That is consistent with the paper's suggestive evidence on ecosystem dynamics, since pathogen transmission itself varies with temperature.`,
    ],
    caveatTitle: "Read percentages against volume",
    caveat: `${n.busiestLabel} carries the largest baseline volume at ${n.busiestBase} visits per 100,000, so even a modest percentage there moves more people than a dramatic percentage on a rare chapter. Use the bars beside the labels.`,
    notesTitle: "What is being estimated",
    notes: [
      "Each chapter is a separate Poisson distributed lag model with 30 lags, fitted to visits assigned to that ICD-10 chapter, and measured against a day between 20 and 25 °C.",
      "Row order is fixed by the cumulative effect of a day below 10 °C and does not change with the controls, so a condition can be followed across states.",
      "Baseline volume is the mean outcome reported in the paper, in visits per 100,000 people. Whiskers are 95% confidence intervals, clustered at the municipality level.",
    ],
    nextLabel: "Next",
    backLabel: "All questions",
  },
  es: {
    eyebrow: self.short.es,
    h1: self.question.es,
    standfirst: `La caída de visitas totales en los días fríos es una cifra neta, y lo neto esconde dos movimientos opuestos. En los 30 días posteriores a un día por debajo de 10 °C, las visitas por ${n.mostDownLabel} caen ${n.mostDown} mientras que las respiratorias suben ${n.respiratory}.`,
    fig1: "Todos los capítulos diagnósticos, en el intervalo y horizonte que elijas",
    readTitle: "Qué leer aquí",
    read: [
      `El agregado no es el panorama operativo. ${n.risingCount} de ${n.totalCount} capítulos suben en los días fríos a 30 días, aunque el total baje. Planear solo con la cifra principal apuntaría a un servicio en la dirección equivocada.`,
      `El capítulo que sube es el respiratorio, y es de alto volumen: ${n.respiratory} en 30 días sobre una base de ${n.respiratoryBase} visitas por 100,000. Un porcentaje sobre un padecimiento común implica una carga absoluta mayor que el mismo porcentaje sobre uno raro, y por eso el volumen base aparece junto a cada etiqueta.`,
      `El mayor porcentaje corresponde a ${n.mostDownLabel}, con ${n.mostDown}. Es consistente con la evidencia sugestiva del artículo sobre dinámicas de ecosistemas, ya que la transmisión de patógenos varía con la temperatura.`,
    ],
    caveatTitle: "Lee los porcentajes contra el volumen",
    caveat: `El capítulo de ${n.busiestLabel} tiene el mayor volumen base, con ${n.busiestBase} visitas por 100,000, así que incluso un porcentaje modesto ahí mueve a más personas que un porcentaje dramático en un capítulo raro. Usa las barras junto a las etiquetas.`,
    notesTitle: "Qué se está estimando",
    notes: [
      "Cada capítulo es un modelo Poisson de rezagos distribuidos con 30 rezagos, ajustado a las visitas asignadas a ese capítulo de la CIE-10, y medido contra un día de entre 20 y 25 °C.",
      "El orden de las filas está fijado por el efecto acumulado de un día por debajo de 10 °C y no cambia con los controles, de modo que se puede seguir un padecimiento entre estados.",
      "El volumen base es la media del resultado reportada en el artículo, en visitas por 100,000 personas. Los bigotes son intervalos de confianza del 95%, agrupados a nivel municipio.",
    ],
    nextLabel: "Siguiente",
    backLabel: "Todas las preguntas",
  },
}[lang];
---

<ModuleRail lang={lang} current="conditions" />

<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
  <header class="max-w-3xl border-b border-rule py-12 sm:py-16">
    <p class="text-[13px] text-slate-light">{strings.eyebrow}</p>
    <h1
      class="mt-3 font-display text-[1.9rem] leading-[1.18] font-semibold text-charcoal sm:text-[2.5rem]"
    >
      {strings.h1}
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-slate-light">
      {strings.standfirst}
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h2 class="font-display text-[1.3rem] leading-snug font-semibold text-charcoal">
      {strings.fig1}
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <RankedChapters lang={lang} />
    </div>
    <DataDownload lang={lang} files={["m4_chapters"]} />
  </section>

  <section class="grid gap-10 border-t border-rule py-12 lg:grid-cols-3 sm:py-16">
    {
      strings.read.map((para) => (
        <p class="border-l-2 border-rule pl-4 text-[14.5px] leading-relaxed text-slate">
          {para}
        </p>
      ))
    }
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-rule py-10">
    <h2 class="font-display text-[1.15rem] font-semibold text-charcoal">
      {strings.caveatTitle}
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-[14.5px] leading-relaxed text-slate-light">
      {strings.caveat}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-rule py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h2 class="text-[13px] font-medium text-slate-light">{strings.notesTitle}</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 grid max-w-5xl gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
      {
        strings.notes.map((para) => (
          <p class="text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-slate-light">{para}</p>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-4 border-t border-rule py-8">
    <a href={SECTION_BASE[lang]} class="text-[14px] text-sky underline underline-offset-4">
      ← {strings.backLabel}
    </a>
    <a
      href={modulePath(next, lang)}
      class="text-[14px] text-sky underline underline-offset-4"
    >
      {strings.nextLabel}: {next.question[lang]} →
    </a>
  </nav>
</div>
